  "Question": "The number halfway between \\(\\dfrac{1}{6}\\) and \\(\\dfrac{1}{4}\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{10}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{5}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{24}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{24}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{12}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The number halfway between two numbers is their average. To find it, add the endpoints and divide by \\(2\\). Using a common denominator first gives\n\\[\n\\frac16+\\frac14=\\frac2{12}+\\frac3{12}=\\frac5{12}.\n\\]\nDividing this sum by \\(2\\), we obtain\n\\[\n\\frac5{12}\\div2=\\frac5{12}\\times\\frac12=\\boxed{\\frac5{24}}.\n\\]\nThis is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
